    "plain": "Hilbert's 10th problem asks: can you algorithmically check if a polynomial equation has integer solutions? MRDP (1970) proved: no, for $\\mathbb{Z}$. But what about the ring of integers of other number fields like $\\mathbb{Q}(\\sqrt{2})$ or $\\mathbb{Q}(\\sqrt{-5})$?",
